  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2016_phy_a35.png\">\r\n\r\nLet when link AB is removed, $x$ is an equivalent of remaining part of cube without link.\r\n\r\nAB and rest part will be in paralel, so according to question\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{c}\r\n\\frac{7}{12}=\\frac{R_{1} R_{2}}{R_{1}+R}=\\frac{1(x)}{1+x}=\\frac{x}{1+x} \\\\\r\n\\frac{7}{12}=\\frac{x}{1+x} \\\\\r\n12 x=7+7 x \\\\\r\n12 x-7 x=7\r\n\\end{array}\r\n5 x=7\r\n$$\r\n$$\r\nx=\\frac{7}{5} \\Omega\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
